Also, this section would especially make sense if some of the gems did more
than just be worth something. For example, blessed dilithium crystals could
be like a ring of regeneration for one's magical energy, and make casting
spells more effective, while cursed dilithium crystals could drain magical
energy. Also, throwing a ruby to an aligned unicorn could reconcile one
automatically with his god. Conversely, throwing a ruby to a non-aligned
unicorn could anger his god. A blessed diamond could ward off nymphs and
other seducers. Dropping a sapphire into potions could uncurse them. These
are just ideas, but it could make gems play a bigger role in the game, and
would make a gem-identifying archeologist a more attractive character. Also,
it would compel the nethacker to identify gems, which I suspect is rarely
done in regular play. One last idea: dropping gems in fountains could
"identify" them a la the trick with rings in sinks, at the cost of perhaps
losing them.

Any comments?
 


